      "id": "frontier-science-60s",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "duration_s": 13.0368,
          "headline": "A question worth making inspectable",
          "id": "question",
          "narration": "Could a biological design be checked as carefully as a program? MorphoSwarm Frontier is an early step toward Lean for biology: shared claims, equations, assumptions and evidence that people and agents can inspect.",
          "start_s": 0.0
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 10.660799999999998,
          "headline": "Published biology supplies hypotheses",
          "id": "hypotheses",
          "narration": "We start with a demanding question: could a zebrafish acquire the structures needed to glide? Published fin-growth genetics supplies hypotheses, not a demonstrated route to flight.",
          "start_s": 13.0368
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 9.0048,
          "headline": "A conditional beam bound, checked",
          "id": "lean",
          "narration": "For a fin modeled as an elastic beam, we formalized a stiffness condition that bounds deflection. Lean compiled the theorem and rejected a corrupted law.",
          "start_s": 23.697599999999998
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 13.720799999999999,
          "headline": "A proof does not establish its premises",
          "id": "boundary",
          "narration": "That checks a mathematical implication; whether the model describes a living fin still requires evidence. The studio connects bounded results across scales and exposes missing links as open questions.",
          "start_s": 32.7024
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 13.576800000000006,
          "headline": "A shared, checkable scientific commons",
          "id": "community",
          "narration": "Through MCP, contributors can retrieve claims, submit work and contest evidence. Our goal is reusable, checkable biology: proof establishes what follows from a model; experiments establish when it applies.",
          "start_s": 46.423199999999994
        }
      ],
      "title": "A conditional foundation for Lean for biology"
    },
